SUMMARY:Deadline: Future Vision XPRIZE (sci-fi film competition)
DESCRIPTION:Future Vision XPRIZE is a sci-fi film competition challenging f
 ilmmakers to portray an optimistic\, abundant future for humanity rather t
 han a dystopian one. CHALLENGE: create a 3-minute sci-fi trailer that depi
 cts a bold\, original\, hopeful vision of progress. PRIZES: USD 3.5 millio
 n-plus total\; the grand prize winner gets USD 2.6 million-plus to turn th
 eir trailer into a feature film\, plus over USD 1 million in prizes for ru
 nners-up. BACKGROUND: launched by the nonprofit XPRIZE and funded by Peter
  Diamandis\, with Google and Range as partners\; inspired by the optimism 
 of Star Trek and intended to give storytellers a hopeful 'north star' for 
 builders. ELIGIBILITY: open to all filmmakers globally. TIMELINE: competit
 ion launched 9 March 2026\; submission deadline 15 August 2026\; finals on
  25 September 2026 in Los Angeles (finalists attend in person). APPLY: reg
 ister and read the rules on the contest website at futurevisionxprize.com.
 \n\nOrganisation: XPRIZE (Future Vision XPRIZE\, funded by Peter Diamandis
 \; partners Google and Range)\nLocation: Online / Worldwide (finals held i
 n Los Angeles)\nAward: USD 3.5 million-plus prize pool. Grand prize winner
  receives USD 2.6 million-plus to develop their vision into a feature film
 \, with over USD 1 million in additional prizes for runners-up.\nDuration:
  One-off competition\; create a 3-minute sci-fi trailer\n\nMore: https://f
 uturevisionxprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://futurevisionxprize.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online / Worldwide (finals held in Los Angeles)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mountainfilm-commitment-grants-emerging-filmmaker-fellowship-2026@artif
 icialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T193951Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260716
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260717
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mountainfilm: Commitment Grants & Emerging Filmmaker Fell
 owship
DESCRIPTION:Mountainfilm's Commitment Grants support documentary filmmakers
  with projects in post-production\, with over USD 90\,000 in funding this 
 cycle for films that celebrate adventure\, activism\, social justice\, cul
 ture\, the environment\, and indomitable spirit. Mountainfilm actively enc
 ourages diversity behind the camera\, and a portion of funding is set asid
 e for two focus areas: projects featuring an LGBTQ+ protagonist or a story
  about overcoming personal challenges\, societal stigmas\, and/or communit
 y obstacles with a meaningful connection to the outdoors or nature-based p
 ursuits\; and projects exploring immigration or migration\, or created by 
 immigrant or first-generation immigrant filmmakers. AWARDS: individual Com
 mitment Grants range from USD 3\,000 to 6\,000. EMERGING FILMMAKER FELLOWS
 HIP: one early-career filmmaker is selected from the Commitment Grant appl
 icant pool for a yearlong mentorship that includes edit and story consulta
 tion\, networking opportunities\, a cash award\, and a funded trip to Tell
 uride during the festival over Memorial Day weekend (travel\, lodging\, an
 d a Mountainfilm pass\, applicable to the year following the award). ELIGI
 BILITY: Commitment Grants are open to applicants from any country\; the Em
 erging Filmmaker Fellowship accepts applicants from any country but requir
 es current U.S. residency. Post-production projects only\, completed\, rel
 eased\, or festival-screened projects are not eligible\, and impact campai
 gns are not funded. Prior Commitment Grant recipients should not re-apply 
 for the same project\; previously declined projects may re-apply only with
  substantial changes. REQUIREMENTS: a video sample or trailer of the curre
 nt project no longer than 10 minutes (password-protected Vimeo links prefe
 rred)\; the screener link must stay active and cannot be changed after sub
 mission. The Emerging Filmmaker application additionally requires a direct
 or bio\, headshot\, and cover letter. Recipients are expected to provide p
 rogress updates 2-3 times a year\, include Mountainfilm recognition in cre
 dits\, and discuss premiere consideration with the programming team. TIMEL
 INE: applications are open July 1 to July 16\, 2026 (closing 11:59 PM MDT)
 \, with notifications in late August or early September. Questions: entrie
 s@mountainfilm.org.\n\nOrganisation: Mountainfilm\nLocation: Application o
 nline\; Telluride\, Colorado\, United States (fellowship trip during the f
 estival). Commitment Grants are open to filmmakers from any country\; the 
 Emerging Filmmaker Fellowship requires current U.S. residency.\nAward: Ove
 r USD 90\,000 in total funding. Individual Commitment Grants range from US
 D 3\,000 to 6\,000. The Emerging Filmmaker Fellowship adds a yearlong ment
 orship\, a cash award\, and a funded trip to Telluride over Memorial Day w
 eekend (travel\, lodging\, and a festival pass).\nDuration: Commitment Gra
 nts support projects in post-production\; the Emerging Filmmaker Fellowshi
 p is a yearlong mentorship.\n\nMore: https://www.mountainfilm.org/mountain
 film-initiatives/commitment-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mountainfilm.org/mountainfilm-initiatives/commitment-grants
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Application online\; Telluride\, Colorado\, United States (fellows
 hip trip during the festival). Commitment Grants are open to filmmakers fr
 om any country\; the Emerging Filmmaker Fellowship requires current U.S. r
 esidency.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:web-residencies-no-22-ignore-all-previous-instructions-2026@artificialn
 ouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T193951Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260807
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260808
SUMMARY:Deadline: Akademie Schloss Solitude: Web Residencies No. 22 - Ignor
 e All Previous Instructions
DESCRIPTION:Web Residencies No. 22\, 'Ignore All Previous Instructions\,' i
 s curated by !Mediengruppe Bitnik as part of Akademie Schloss Solitude's W
 eb Residencies program\, which since 2016 has supported young talents from
  the international digital scene as well as artists of all disciplines eng
 aging with web-based practices. For the tenth anniversary of the program\,
  this edition invites artists to create works that challenge extractive di
 gital platforms and AI systems\, exploring how to interrupt dominant techn
 ological logics\, from ad-tech surveillance to prompt injection vulnerabil
 ities\, and imagine alternative structures and communication methods. The 
 open call seeks proposals that hijack\, glitch\, and disrupt rather than c
 omply with existing systems\, drawing on strategies like Situationist deto
 urnement to map routes through and around the grids we are trapped within.
  Four to six proposals will be selected. BENEFITS: a four-week online resi
 dency\; a grant of EUR 1\,200\; a web space (microsite) on which the proje
 ct can be developed and published online\; support from a web/UX designer 
 and a programmer (in a supportive capacity only\, not to build an entire w
 ebsite)\; and participation in individual and group online events with the
  curators and Solitude fellows. Offline or hybrid formats (a reading sessi
 on\, panel\, exhibition\, or curated program) may follow. ELIGIBILITY: art
 ists of all disciplines may apply\, with no age limit\; submission is free
  of charge. The residency takes place exclusively online\, and selected fe
 llows agree to be available online during the four weeks. TIMELINE: the op
 en call runs from July 7 to August 7\, 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Akademie Sch
 loss Solitude\nLocation: Online (fully remote). Awarded by Akademie Schlos
 s Solitude\, Stuttgart\, Germany.\nAward: EUR 1\,200 grant for a four-week
  online residency\, plus a microsite to develop and publish the project\, 
 and support from a web/UX designer and a programmer in a supportive capaci
 ty.\nDuration: Four-week online residency.\n\nMore: https://application.ak
 ademie-solitude.de/fellowship-information/web-residencies?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://application.akademie-solitude.de/fellowship-information/web-res
 idencies?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (fully remote). Awarded by Akademie Schloss Solitude\, Stut
 tgart\, Germany.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:doc-society-climate-story-fund-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T193951Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260824
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260825
SUMMARY:Deadline: Doc Society: Climate Story Fund
DESCRIPTION:The Doc Society Climate Story Fund\, run by Doc Society's Clima
 te Story Unit\, provides grants of up to USD 125\,000 to support non-ficti
 on projects in late production and the implementation of impact campaigns 
 for both completed and in-production projects. The fund supports compellin
 g independent media storytelling and impact strategies aligned with the Fu
 nd's mission around climate justice and biodiversity. This call has no set
  theme\, welcoming applications across all areas aligned with the Fund's m
 ission. Since 2021 the fund has distributed more than USD 4M to over 50 pr
 ojects\, with grantee work reaching distribution through outlets including
  BBC\, POV\, Netflix\, Hulu\, Disney+\, Spotify\, YouTube\, and WhatsApp. 
 WHAT YOU GET: up to USD 125\,000 to support non-fiction projects in late p
 roduction and impact campaigns. WHO IS ELIGIBLE: open to filmmakers of any
  nationality. DEADLINE: 24 August 2026. TO APPLY: see the fund page and ap
 ply via the Doc Society application. Questions: climate@docsociety.org.\n\
 nOrganisation: Doc Society (Climate Story Unit)\nLocation: Remote / intern
 ational. Open to filmmakers of any nationality.\nAward: Grants of up to US
 D 125\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Supports late-production of non
 -fiction projects and the implementation of impact campaigns for completed
  and in-production projects.\n\nMore: https://climatestoryunit.org/fund/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://climatestoryunit.org/fund/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / international. Open to filmmakers of any nationality.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prospect-art-new-work-we-come-in-pieces-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260902T193951Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:Deadline: Prospect Art: NEW WORK Commission 2027 - "We Come in Piec
 es"
DESCRIPTION:Prospect Art invites visual artists worldwide to apply for the 
 2027 NEW WORK commission\, a USD 1\,500 project grant supporting the creat
 ion of a new\, conceptually driven work responding to the curatorial theme
  "We Come in Pieces\," developed by 2026-2027 Curatorial Fellow Alma Samme
 l. Through a single application\, artists are also considered for ONE WORK
  (an online series featuring an in-depth conversation centered on a single
  completed artwork) and BROADCAST (a curated online program of screenings\
 , artist talks\, and discussions). THEME: "We Come in Pieces" proposes the
  Alien as a method for shifting perspective\, approaching alienness as a p
 ractice of estrangement to encounter the world beyond familiar human-cente
 red narratives. It explores relationships between human and more-than-huma
 n worlds\, speculative cosmologies\, ecological systems\, technologies\, l
 andscapes\, histories\, infrastructures\, and nonhuman forms of intelligen
 ce (satellites and orbital debris\, fungal networks\, oceans\, atmospheric
  systems\, algorithmic intelligences)\, inviting works that displace the p
 oint of listening\, seeing\, sensing\, or knowing. Research-based and conc
 eptually driven practices are especially encouraged. WHAT'S OFFERED: NEW W
 ORK\, USD 1\,500 to one artist plus a featured website section and social 
 promotion (project completed within 12 months)\; ONE WORK\, a published ar
 ticle and social promotion\; BROADCAST\, a USD 125 screening or speaking f
 ee and inclusion in a themed program. ELIGIBILITY: professional visual art
 ists working in any medium at any career stage\, except those currently en
 rolled in undergraduate or graduate studio art programs\; collectives may 
 apply. Media welcomed include moving image\, installation\, sculpture\, ph
 otography\, performance\, sound\, digital media\, social practice\, and in
 terdisciplinary forms. APPLICATION: submit via the official Google Form wi
 th contact information\, a project description (250 words)\, a sketch/visu
 alization (1-3 images)\, up to 3 links to completed work samples\, a state
 ment relating the project to the theme (200 words)\, a short bio and exhib
 ition history (500 words)\, and a budget breakdown of the USD 1\,500. A US
 D 10 administrative fee is paid via PayPal (include PayPal name and transa
 ction ID)\; a fee waiver is available with no explanation by emailing subm
 issions@prospectart.org before the deadline. Writers may email gioj@prospe
 ctart.org with samples. DEADLINE: 16 August 2026\; results for the NEW WOR
 K grant notified by end of September. INFO SESSION: 5 August 2026 at noon 
 PST.\n\nOrganisation: Prospect Art\nLocation: Remote / online. Open to vis
 ual artists worldwide\; programs (ONE WORK\, BROADCAST) run online.\nAward
 : NEW WORK: USD 1\,500 commission for one artist\, plus a featured website
  section and social promotion. BROADCAST: USD 125 screening or speaking fe
 e if selected. ONE WORK: a published article (exposure). NOTE: a USD 10 ad
 ministrative fee applies to apply\, with a no-questions-asked waiver avail
 able on request before the deadline. PayPal account required to receive fu
 nds.\nDuration: The commissioned NEW WORK project should be completed with
 in twelve months of selection.\n\nMore: https://www.prospectart.org/new-wo
 rk-grant?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.prospectart.org/new-work-grant?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / online. Open to visual artists worldwide\; programs (ONE 
 WORK\, BROADCAST) run online.
END:VEVENT
