UID:hiding-in-plain-site-festival-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T193951Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Hiding in Plain Site: International Public Art Short Film
  Festival
DESCRIPTION:Hiding in Plain Site is an international public art short film 
 festival accepting film\, video art\, XR\, and explicitly AI-generated or 
 AI-assisted moving image works of 2 to 20 minutes\, screened in public spa
 ce. Free to submit\; selected filmmakers receive a modest stipend whose am
 ount is revenue-dependent and not yet confirmed. Deadline 10 September 202
 6.\n\nOrganisation: Hiding in Plain Site\nLocation: United States / online
 \; screenings sited in public space. Open internationally.\nAward: Screeni
 ng\; selected filmmakers receive a modest stipend (amount to be confirmed\
 , revenue-dependent). Free to submit.\nDuration: Short films 2-20 minutes\
 ; festival screens work in public sites.\n\nMore: https://www.hidinginplai
 nsite.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.hidinginplainsite.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States / online\; screenings sited in public space. Open in
 ternationally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:flickr-bwp-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T193951Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260806
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260807
SUMMARY:Deadline: Flickr x Black Women Photographers Grant 2026 (Traces of 
 Connection)
DESCRIPTION:Flickr and Black Women Photographers award a USD 10\,000 grant 
 to a Black female or non-binary photographer to invest in their practice. 
 The 2026 edition centers on the theme Traces of Connection\, chosen by 202
 5 recipient and guest judge Eleonore Menga. TO APPLY: be a member of the B
 lack Women Photographers organization (free)\, join the BWP Flickr Communi
 ty\, submit one photograph inspired by the theme to the community\, and sh
 are a brief description of how the image connects to it. The winner also r
 eceives a two-year Flickr Pro and a one-year SmugMug Pro membership\, and 
 is announced live at the first MODE by Flickr festival in Minneapolis (18-
 20 September 2026)\; ten additional recipients receive Flickr Pro and Smug
 Mug Pro memberships. DEADLINE: 6 August 2026. No entry fee.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Flickr and Black Women Photographers (BWP)\nLocation: Open internationa
 lly to Black female and non-binary photographers\; winner announced at the
  MODE by Flickr festival in Minneapolis\, USA (18-20 September 2026).\nAwa
 rd: USD 10\,000 grant to invest in the recipient's practice\, plus a two-y
 ear Flickr Pro and one-year SmugMug Pro membership\; ten additional recipi
 ents each receive one-year Flickr Pro and SmugMug Pro memberships. No entr
 y fee (BWP membership is free).\nDuration: Winner announced live at MODE b
 y Flickr\, 18-20 September 2026\n\nMore: https://blackwomenphotographers.c
 om/smugmug-flickr?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://blackwomenphotographers.com/smugmug-flickr?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Open internationally to Black female and non-binary photographers\
 ; winner announced at the MODE by Flickr festival in Minneapolis\, USA (18
 -20 September 2026).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art-explora-cite-internationale-des-arts-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260902T193951Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261106
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261107
SUMMARY:Deadline: Art Explora x Cite internationale des arts Residency Prog
 ramme\, 2027 Sessions
DESCRIPTION:Residency programme run by the Art Explora Foundation with the 
 Cite internationale des arts at its Montmartre site\, supporting work that
  engages scientific and technological exploration and the major social and
  environmental issues of the present. Residents receive a studio-apartment
  of around 50 sqm\, a monthly living grant of EUR 1\,000\, a production gr
 ant of up to EUR 3\,000\, and a round-trip travel grant\, plus access to p
 roduction facilities and local networks. Two tracks are offered: a SOLO pr
 ogramme for artists and writers across visual arts\, performance\, digital
  practices\, literary and other experimental disciplines\, and a COLLECTIV
 E programme for duos or collectives working collaboratively on interdiscip
 linary\, experimental or research-based projects\, for which a single stud
 io-apartment designed for collaborative work hosts two residents sharing a
  bed\, and only one member should submit the application. Eligible artisti
 c disciplines are visual arts\, performance and live arts\, digital arts\,
  curatorial practices\, and writing and literary practices\; eligible rese
 arch fields are humanities\, social sciences\, cultural studies and histor
 y\, technological innovation\, and ecology. No output is required at the e
 nd of the residency\, but participation in the Open Studios is mandatory. 
 ELIGIBILITY: artists\, artist collectives\, researchers\, curators and wri
 ters of all nationalities\, no age restriction\, with a minimum of five ye
 ars of professional activity and works or research exhibited at national o
 r international level. The Cite lists 20 to 22 residencies per year on thi
 s programme. Deadline 6 November 2026\, 23:59 Europe/Paris. Questions: res
 idences@artexplora.org. FLAG: the grant figures above come from the open-c
 all text supplied to the desk\; neither the Cite nor Art Explora publishes
  amounts on the programme page\, so confirm them\, along with the exact de
 adline\, before applying.\n\nOrganisation: Art Explora Foundation with the
  Cite internationale des arts\nLocation: Paris\, France (Cite internationa
 le des arts\, Montmartre site\, 24 rue Norvins\, 75018). Open to applicant
 s of all nationalities with no age restriction.\nAward: Monthly living gra
 nt of EUR 1\,000\, production grant of up to EUR 3\,000\, a round-trip tra
 vel grant\, and a fully equipped studio-apartment of roughly 50 sqm. For c
 ollectives and duos the living grant (up to EUR 2\,000) and the production
  grant (up to EUR 3\,000) are shared between members. Access to production
  facilities and local networks. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 to 6 mont
 hs. Session 1: March to August 2027. Session 2: September 2027 to February
  2028.\n\nMore: https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/en/programme-de-r
 esidence/art-explora-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.citeinternationaledesarts.fr/en/programme-de-residence/art-
 explora-x-cite-internationale-des-arts/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Cite internationale des arts\, Montmartre site\, 2
 4 rue Norvins\, 75018). Open to applicants of all nationalities with no ag
 e restriction.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:artist-grant-unrestricted-1200-november-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260902T193951Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Artist Grant: Unrestricted $1\,200 Visual Artist Grant (N
 ovember 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Artist Grant awards an unrestricted USD 1\,200 grant to one vis
 ual artist three times a year\, on a deliberately low-friction application
 : NO grant proposal is required. You email a link to your website\, or 3-5
  images of your work as JPG\, PNG or PDF\, plus a resume\, CV or short bio
  with your name\, to submit@artistgrant.org\, and separately pay the USD 3
 0 fee through Stripe or PayPal. If the name on your payment differs from t
 he name on your email\, say so in the email. ELIGIBILITY: visual artists a
 ged 18 or over\, worldwide. Past winners may NOT apply again. MEDIA ACCEPT
 ED: painting\, drawing\, sculpture\, ceramics\, printmaking\, photography\
 , mixed media\, installation\, and new or alternative visual art forms. NO
 T ACCEPTED: film and video\, music\, theatre\, dance. SELECTION CRITERIA: 
 a cohesive body of work\; well-crafted work\; well-presented work\, judged
  with an explicit allowance that artists have differing financial means fo
 r presentation\; work that communicates its viewpoint\, ideas and concepts
  clearly\, effectively and creatively\; and work that is not derivative. R
 ESULTS: all applicants are notified within 6-8 weeks of each deadline\, an
 d results are announced on the website\, social media and newsletter. They
  will not respond to individual queries during the review period. VISIBILI
 TY: grantees are showcased on the website\, social media and marketing mat
 erials\, and selected applicants are featured on social media with permiss
 ion. Artists retain their copyrights. NOTE: the grant recurs on 15 March\,
  15 July and 15 November each year\, and this desk lists each round separa
 tely. There is a USD 30 application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Artist Grant\nLo
 cation: Remote (worldwide). No residency or travel component.\nAward: Unre
 stricted USD 1\,200 grant to one visual artist per round\, awarded three t
 imes a year. Application fee of USD 30\, paid separately via Stripe or Pay
 Pal.\nDuration: One-off unrestricted award\; no reporting or project perio
 d\n\nMore: https://artistgrant.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artistgrant.org/apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote (worldwide). No residency or travel component.
END:VEVENT
